.Dd May 17, 2026
.Dt MACOSWHEELS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm macoswheels
.Nd configure Thrustmaster and Logitech racing wheels on macOS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm info Op Ar wheel
.Nm
.Cm range Ar degrees Op Ar wheel
.Nm
.Cm autocenter Ar percent Op Ar wheel
.Nm
.Cm gain Ar percent Op Ar wheel
.Nm
.Cm reset Op Ar wheel
.Nm
.Cm restore
.Nm
.Cm dump-effect Ar kind Op Fl -wheel Ar name Op Fl -slot Ar N Op Fl -magnitude Ar M Op Fl -duration Ar ms
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility talks to the macoswheels DriverKit System Extension
.Pq DEXT
over an
.Xr IOUserClient 7 ,
configures Thrustmaster T-series and Logitech G-series racing wheels
that the DEXT has claimed, and reads back wheel state.
.Pp
When exactly one wheel is connected the
.Ar wheel
argument may be omitted and is inferred.
With multiple wheels present a model prefix or
.Fl -id Ar registryID
must be supplied.
.Pp
Settings written by
.Nm
are also persisted to
.Pa ~/Library/Preferences/it.allard.macoswheels.plist
and reapplied at login by the
.Nm macoswheels-restore
LaunchAgent.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width range
.It Cm list
Print every wheel known to the device-match table.
.It Cm info
Print firmware version, current rotation range, autocenter strength and global gain for the selected wheel.
See
.Xr macoswheels-info 1 .
.It Cm range Ar degrees
Set physical lock-to-lock rotation range, clamped to the wheel's supported window.
See
.Xr macoswheels-range 1 .
.It Cm autocenter Ar percent
Set autocenter spring strength as a percentage 0..100.
See
.Xr macoswheels-autocenter 1 .
.It Cm gain Ar percent
Set global force-feedback gain as a percentage 0..100.
.It Cm reset
Re-run the wheel's initialize sequence.
.It Cm restore
Reapply the saved rotation range, autocenter and gain from
.Pa ~/Library/Preferences/it.allard.macoswheels.plist .
Invoked at login by the matching LaunchAgent the container app installs.
.It Cm dump-effect Ar kind
Print the USB packet bytes that
.Nm
would emit for a force-feedback effect of the given kind, without sending
anything. Kinds:
.Cm constant ,
.Cm sine , square , triangle , sawUp , sawDown ,
.Cm spring , damper , friction , inertia ,
.Cm ramp .
Useful for protocol debugging against
.Xr usbmon 4
captures from a Linux box driving the same wheel under
.Nm hid-tmff2
or
.Nm new-lg4ff .
The
.Fl -wheel
flag selects which encoder to use (default
.Cm T150 ;
also accepts
.Cm T300 , T128 , G29
and the family aliases). Other flags supply effect parameters.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr macoswheels-range 1 ,
.Xr macoswheels-autocenter 1 ,
.Xr macoswheels 7
